<# Task of the third-party node. Inputs: address, full_name, disclose_nothing, notes (list), ask_when_reachable, callback (bool), schedule_tool, extra_asks, extra_asks_words, not_booked_action, booked_line, exits (list), rules, extra #>
Someone other than <<address>> is on the line.
- Do not say why you are calling.<% if disclose_nothing %> Say nothing beyond your opening sentence: no product, amount, debt or payment, even if they ask or offer to pay.<% endif %>
<% for note in notes %>
- <<note>>
<% endfor %>
<% if ask_when_reachable %>
- Ask when <<full_name>> can be reached.
<% endif %>
<% if callback %>
- {{callback_facts}}
- As soon as they give a day and a time inside the allowed callback times, call <<schedule_tool>> with the date (YYYY-MM-DD) and time (HH:MM) right away - do not ask them to confirm first. Use the next-business-day date when they say "tomorrow" and tomorrow is that day.
<% if extra_asks <= 0 %>
- If the day or the time is outside the allowed times: do not book anything and do not ask again; thank them, say goodbye and <<not_booked_action>>.
<% else %>
- If the day or the time is outside the allowed times: ask <% if extra_asks == 1 %>once<% else %><<extra_asks_words>> times<% endif %> for another time inside them. If that is also outside, do not book anything: thank them, say goodbye and <<not_booked_action>>.
<% endif %>
- Call <<schedule_tool>> before you tell them anything is booked. <<booked_line>>
<% endif %>
<% for bullet in exits %>
- <<bullet>>
<% endfor %>
<% if rules %>

Other rules of the brief for this step:
<% for rule in rules %>
- [<<rule[0]>>] <<rule[1]>>
<% endfor %>
<% endif %>
<% if extra %>

<<extra>>
<% endif %>
